<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <AssemblyName>SwissEphSharp</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>SwissEphNet</RootNamespace>
    <PackageId>SwissEphSharp</PackageId>
    <!--
      Version scheme: upstream Swiss Ephemeris version + port revision, e.g.
      2.10.3 tracks Swiss Ephemeris C 2.10.03 (upstream tag v2.10.3final),
      the version the port itself now targets end to end: SE_VERSION,
      sweph.c, swecl.c, swehouse.c and swetest.c have all landed. This is
      the version intended for the first nuget.org release, under the
      SwissEphSharp package ID. It cannot go out under SwissEphNet: 2.8.0.2
      already holds that ID, and the library no longer ships
      net40/netstandard1.0, so it would not be a drop-in replacement for
      that package anyway. Until the release lands, build from source or
      reference the project directly.

      The "port revision" above is the fourth component, for a fork-only
      release made while upstream stays put: 2.10.3, then 2.10.3.1, 2.10.3.2,
      resetting whenever upstream moves. Two things to know before using it.
      NuGet normalizes a trailing zero away, so 2.10.3.0 and 2.10.3 are the
      same package and there is no point writing the .0. That was measured,
      not assumed: packing 2.10.3.0 produces a .2.10.3.nupkg. And four components
      are not valid SemVer 2.0, which has exactly three; NuGet accepts them
      for backwards compatibility. That is a deliberate choice, because the
      alternatives are worse. Build metadata (2.10.3+fork.1) is ignored by
      NuGet when comparing versions, so a second package differing only there
      cannot be published. A prerelease suffix (2.10.3-rev1) sorts BEFORE
      2.10.3, which is backwards for a release that comes after it.
    -->
    <Version>2.10.3</Version>
    <!--
      Plain SemVer, with no descriptive text. The SDK appends +<commit sha> to
      whatever is here, so anything with spaces or parentheses in the core
      version produces a string no SemVer parser accepts, and several tools
      do parse AssemblyInformationalVersionAttribute. It is also what Windows
      Explorer shows as "Product version". The upstream tracking detail this
      used to carry now lives in the AssemblyMetadata items below, which is
      where arbitrary text belongs.
    -->
    <InformationalVersion>2.10.3</InformationalVersion>
    <Authors>Yan Grenier, Timothy van der Ham</Authors>
    <!--
      Company is the publisher field, distinct from Authors above: NuGet shows it separately, and
      it should name whoever is actually publishing this package, not the original author of the
      code it is a fork of. This fork is published by Timothy van der Ham; Yan Grenier is credited
      in Authors, Copyright and NOTICE, which is where authorship attribution belongs. Setting
      Company to Yan Grenier here would sit awkwardly next to Description's own "Not published or
      endorsed by Yan Grenier" line below.
    -->
    <Company>Timothy van der Ham</Company>
    <Product>SwissEphSharp</Product>
    <Title>SwissEphSharp</Title>
    <Description>Swiss Ephemeris .Net portage. SwissEphSharp is the package ID this project is distributed under: a fork of Yan Grenier's SwissEphNet, tracking Swiss Ephemeris 2.10.03. The assembly is now named SwissEphSharp too, so it can coexist with the original SwissEphNet package; the namespace stays SwissEphNet, so source that only uses the public API needs no changes beyond the PackageReference itself. Callers of the removed OnLoadFile event still need to migrate to SwissEph.FileProvider. Not published or endorsed by Yan Grenier or Astrodienst.</Description>
    <Copyright>Copyright (C) 1997-2021 Astrodienst AG; (C) 2014-2019 Yan Grenier; (C) 2026 Timothy van der Ham</Copyright>
    <PackageLicenseUrl></PackageLicenseUrl>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/Tim81/SwissEphNet</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/Tim81/SwissEphNet</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PackageTags>Swiss Ephemeris</PackageTags>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>2.10.3 (the first release of this fork published to nuget.org, under the
SwissEphSharp package ID; entries from 2.8.0.2 down are the original project's, published under
SwissEphNet):
- SE_VERSION now reports "2.10.03", matching the C library this port tracks (upstream tag
  v2.10.3final). Every stage of the 2.10.03 delta has landed: the header/constants stage,
  swephlib.c, the ayanamsha machinery, sweph.c, swecl.c, swehouse.c and swetest.c.
- swe_houses, swe_houses_ex, swe_houses_armc, swe_house_pos and swe_house_name each gained an
  int hsys overload alongside the existing char hsys overload, matching upstream swephexp.h.
- New API surface: swe_houses_ex2, swe_houses_armc_ex2, swe_calc_pctr, swe_get_current_file_data.
- OnLoadFile is gone; ephemeris files are read from disk by default through the new
  SwissEph.FileProvider (IEphemerisFileProvider).
- The assembly is now named SwissEphSharp (was SwissEphNet), so this package can coexist in one
  dependency graph with the original SwissEphNet 2.8.0.2 instead of silently colliding with it at
  build time and crashing at runtime. The namespace stays SwissEphNet.
- 2.10.3 is the last release to ship netstandard2.0; net8.0 or later will be required starting
  with the next release. Consumers on .NET Framework 4.6.1+ can still take 2.10.3, but should
  not expect the one after it to carry netstandard2.0. netstandard2.0 is a compatibility target,
  not a correctness one: measured on .NET Framework 4.8 against .NET 10, the same asset's
  swe_calc differs on 21 of 111 calls (37 bodies, 3 epochs; worst case SE_TRUE_NODE longitude
  speed, 1.33e-7 relative), while net8.0 and net10.0 agree on all 111. The cause is .NET
  Framework 4.8's less accurate Math.Sin/Math.Tan near pi, not this port; see the "V:2.10.3"
  section of README.md for the full measurement.
- Numerous port bug fixes surfaced by the 2.10.03 work, several of them upstream C bugs Astrodienst
  fixed between 2.08 and 2.10.03 that this port now also carries: swe_nod_aps/swe_nod_aps_ut
  returning all-zero nodes and apsides, an obliquity read that affected every SEFLG_SWIEPH
  position, eclipse magnitude and obscuration off by a factor of 100, and the swe_house_pos buffer
  that was one element short for Gauquelin houses. See docs/compliance-2.10.03.md for the
  verification numbers behind this release and docs/known-issues.md and the "V:2.10.3" section
  of README.md for the full list.

2.8.1.0 (not published to nuget.org; source-only distribution):
- Package ID renamed from SwissEphNet to SwissEphSharp. SwissEphNet on nuget.org belongs to the
  upstream author's own release and this fork cannot publish under it. At this release the
  assembly name and namespace were unaffected: both stayed SwissEphNet, so the only change a
  consumer needed to make was the PackageReference itself. The assembly was renamed too, later,
  at 2.10.3 above -- see that entry and the "Package name" section of README.md.
- Retarget the library to netstandard2.0;net8.0;net10.0, dropping net40 and netstandard1.0.
- Relicense from GPL-2.0-or-later to the Swiss Ephemeris 2.10.3 dual license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
  or a Swiss Ephemeris Professional License from Astrodienst. See LICENSE and NOTICE.
- Fix SwissEph.DIR_GLUE: was hardcoded to '\\' on every platform, now '/' per the upstream C
  source. Asteroid file names passed to OnLoadFile change accordingly, e.g. "ast4/se04179.se1"
  instead of "ast4\se04179.se1".
- Fix SwissEph.DefaultEncoding: was falling back to UTF-8 silently whenever Windows-1252 could
  not be resolved (missing System.Text.Encoding.CodePages reference); UTF-8 is now the explicit,
  deliberate default, matching the actual encoding of the ephemeris data files.
  You can still override it via the static SwissEphNet.SwissEph.DefaultEncoding property.
- Fix C.strcmp/strncmp/strstr/strchr: were culture-sensitive (string.Compare/IndexOf), now
  ordinal, matching C's byte-wise semantics. Affects fixed-star name search/sort under
  non-invariant cultures.
- Several additional port bug fixes with no signature change: swe_fixstar multi-word star names
  and an off-by-one in search-name formatting, a missing ref-parameter mutation and missing guard
  in the heliacal Moon branch, swe_set_astro_models throwing on short input, C.atoi sign handling,
  CPointer&lt;T&gt;.operator != always returning false, and a netstandard2.0-only infinite
  recursion in a string-extension method. See NOTICE and docs/known-issues.md for details.

2.8.0.2:
- Fix the #41 issue

2.8.0.1:
- Update to version 2.08 of SwissEphemeris

2.7.1.3:
- Update to version 2.07.1 of SwissEphemeris
- Inlcude the PR #34 - swe_house_pos: parameter geolon is actually geolat - thanks to aleksamagicka

2.6.0.24:
- Include the PR #32 - Make fixed star name parameter ref  - thanks to aleksamagicka

2.6.0.23:
- Fix the #29 issue

2.6.0.22:
- Fix the #27 issue

2.6.0.21:
- Update to VS 2017 project

2.6.0.18:
- Update the code to the Swiss Ephemeris 2.06.00 version.
</PackageReleaseNotes>
    <NeutralLanguage>en</NeutralLanguage>
    <!--
      Deliberately PackageLicenseFile, not PackageLicenseExpression. NuGet only
      accepts OSI/FSF-approved SPDX identifiers in PackageLicenseExpression, and
      the Swiss Ephemeris Professional License arm of this dual license has no
      SPDX identifier, so the dual license cannot be expressed that way. Do not
      "fix" this to PackageLicenseExpression=AGPL-3.0-or-later: that would drop
      the Professional option from the package metadata and misrepresent the
      license under which this library is actually offered. See LICENSE and
      NOTICE for the real terms.
    -->
    <PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE</PackageLicenseFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)|$(Platform)'=='Debug|AnyCPU'">
    <DefineConstants>TRACE;DEBUG;</DefineConstants>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)|$(Platform)'=='Release|AnyCPU'">
    <DefineConstants>TRACE;RELEASE;</DefineConstants>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    The upstream tracking detail that InformationalVersion used to carry.
    AssemblyMetadata takes arbitrary text without having to parse as a version.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <AssemblyMetadata Include="UpstreamSwissEphemerisVersion" Value="2.10.03" />
    <AssemblyMetadata Include="UpstreamSwissEphemerisTag" Value="v2.10.3final" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    StringExtensions and TypeExtensions are internal (see the remarks on each type):
    these three assemblies call them directly rather than only through the CPort code
    that already sits inside this assembly.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="SwissEphNet.Tests" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="NetStandard20Smoke.Tests" />
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="SweTest" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="..\LICENSE">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath></PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="..\agpl-3.0.txt">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath></PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="..\NOTICE">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath></PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="..\README.md">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath></PackagePath>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>
  
</Project>
